00:00:23,060 --> 00:00:27,380
simple infractional distillations, then please do so before watching this video.

2
00:00:28,100 --> 00:00:33,700
If you have, then you know that simple distillation is an effective technique for purifying liquids.

3
00:00:34,420 --> 00:00:41,460
If the liquids boil below about 150 degrees Celsius, if you have to purify a higher boiling liquid

4
00:00:41,460 --> 00:00:48,260
however, then you must perform a distillation under vacuum. The third type of distillation is

5
00:00:48,260 --> 00:00:54,260
a vacuum distillation. This technique must be used if the liquid boils above about 150 degrees

6
00:00:54,260 --> 00:01:00,260
Celsius, where it is likely to decompose. As you know, the boiling point of a liquid occurs when

7
00:01:00,260 --> 00:01:05,220
its vapor pressure is equal to the external pressure. If a system is under vacuum, it has

8
00:01:05,220 --> 00:01:10,500
a reduced pressure and the liquid is able to boil at a lower temperature. To set up the apparatus

9
00:01:10,500 --> 00:01:16,100
for the vacuum distillation, insert a Claisen adapter between the distillation flask and head.

10
00:01:16,100 --> 00:01:20,980
Liquids often boil violently under reduced pressure and the Claisen adapter is used to

11
00:01:20,980 --> 00:01:26,020
decrease the probability that liquid will bump into the condenser. Instead of using a vacuum

12
00:01:26,020 --> 00:01:31,540
adapter, attach a cow or pig to the end of the condenser and place a receiving flask on each

13
00:01:31,540 --> 00:01:36,900
joint. Because the system will be under vacuum during the distillation, you will not be able

14
00:01:36,900 --> 00:01:42,340
to replace the receiving flask as you did during atmospheric distillation. A cow or pig

15
00:01:42,340 --> 00:01:46,980
allows you to keep the system under vacuum, but still switch to new receiving flasks.

16
00:01:47,620 --> 00:01:52,100
Next, attach heavy walled vacuum tubing to the outlet on the cow or pig adapter.

17
00:01:52,660 --> 00:01:56,340
If the walls of the tubing are too thin, then they will collapse under vacuum.

18
00:01:57,060 --> 00:02:02,260
Attach the other end of the vacuum tubing to a vacuum source, such as a vacuum pump or water

19
00:02:02,260 --> 00:02:07,780
aspirator. The vacuum source should also be connected to a manometer, a device that measures

20
00:02:07,780 --> 00:02:13,620
pressure. Finally, make sure that all joints are greased well. If they're not, solvent may get

21
00:02:13,620 --> 00:02:19,060
into the joints and freeze them shut under vacuum. Apply a thin film of grease to the top of the

22
00:02:19,060 --> 00:02:24,580
male adapter and twist the female adapter onto it until this film of grease can be seen all

23
00:02:24,580 --> 00:02:30,020
around the joint. Do not apply too much grease to the joint and never apply grease close to

24
00:02:30,020 --> 00:02:35,060
the bottom of the male adapter. These actions may cause the grease to seep into the distilling

25
00:02:35,060 --> 00:02:40,980
flask and contaminate your liquid. Before performing a vacuum distillation, you must check for leaks in

26
00:02:40,980 --> 00:02:46,260
your system. To do this, make sure that all of the stopcocks are closed and to turn on the vacuum.

27
00:02:46,900 --> 00:02:52,500
Then, open the stopcocks one by one, starting from the one that is closest to the vacuum source.

28
00:02:53,140 --> 00:02:57,780
As each stopcock is opened, listen for a hissing noise, which implies a leak in the system.

29
00:02:58,420 --> 00:03:02,660
If you find the leak, turn off the vacuum, introduce air into the system,

30
00:03:02,660 --> 00:03:08,340
re-grease the joints, and try again. The system must be free from leaks before you can proceed.

31
00:03:08,340 --> 00:03:12,900
Once you are convinced that the system is free from leaks, fill the solvent trap with liquid

32
00:03:12,900 --> 00:03:18,180
nitrogen. This step is essential to prevent destruction of the vacuum pump by vaporized

33
00:03:18,180 --> 00:03:23,700
solvent. Then, transfer the liquid mixture into the distilling flask and add a stir bar. Do not

34
00:03:23,700 --> 00:03:28,660
add boiling stones for a vacuum distillation. Boiling stones are useless because the vacuum

35
00:03:28,660 --> 00:03:33,540
removes the air in their pores. Move the heating mantle up to the distilling flask and place a

36
00:03:33,540 --> 00:03:39,380
stir plate underneath. Do not turn on the heat. The first step in conducting a vacuum distillation

37
00:03:39,380 --> 00:03:43,940
is turning on the stir plate. If stirring is not occurring during a vacuum distillation,

38
00:03:43,940 --> 00:03:50,500
the probability of bumping increases dramatically. Next, slowly and carefully, introduce the system

39
00:03:50,500 --> 00:03:55,860
to vacuum. You will see the solution start to boil as low boiling impurities and air run

40
00:03:55,860 --> 00:04:01,300
through the apparatus without heat. After the liquid mixture has stopped boiling, turn on the

41
00:04:01,300 --> 00:04:06,740
heat. When the distillation has been started, you can determine the temperature at which the solution

42
00:04:06,740 --> 00:04:12,340
will boil under the reduced pressure conditions through the use of a nomograph. First, find the

43
00:04:12,340 --> 00:04:17,780
boiling point of the compound at atmospheric pressure on line B of the nomograph. Note the

44
00:04:17,780 --> 00:04:22,420
current pressure of your system from the manometer and mark its location on line C of the

45
00:04:22,500 --> 00:04:28,420
nomograph. Using a ruler or straight edge, line up these two points and find the point of intersection

46
00:04:28,420 --> 00:04:34,180
on line A. This number should be a good estimate of your expected boiling point. Carry out the

47
00:04:34,180 --> 00:04:39,060
vacuum distillation as normal. When finished, remove the heat source from the distillation

48
00:04:39,060 --> 00:04:44,820
flask, turn off the vacuum, and allow the solution to cool completely. Then, introduce

49
00:04:44,820 --> 00:04:50,020
air into the system, stop the stirring, and remove the receiving flask. Other things to

50
00:04:50,020 --> 00:04:55,700
remember when carrying out vacuum distillations are as follows. If you know that you have some low

51
00:04:55,700 --> 00:05:00,740
boiling liquid present in your mixture, first carry out a simple distillation to collect it

52
00:05:00,740 --> 00:05:06,500
before attaching the vacuum. If you must separate compounds with similar boiling points, then you

53
00:05:06,500 --> 00:05:10,820
can insert a fractionating column between the distillation flask and Claisen adapter.

54
00:05:11,380 --> 00:05:16,420
Unlike distillations at atmospheric pressure where a narrow boiling point range is observed,

55
00:05:16,420 --> 00:05:22,340
it is not unusual to see a 10 to 20 degree Celsius temperature range during a vacuum distillation

56
00:05:22,340 --> 00:05:28,660
due to pressure changes. Vacuum distillation allows you to purify high boiling liquids

57
00:05:28,660 --> 00:05:32,740
in a reasonable time period without having to worry about decomposition.
